{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BJY3xoGT97WwcGC9RaM5N1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 6 existing tests and 12 new subtests pass. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n**Created `pkg/testutils/normalize_test.go`** with two test functions:\n\n- **`TestTimestampNormalizer`** (7 subtests) — verifies R4.2:\n  - AC2: syslog format (`\"Feb 19 12:34:56\"`) replaced with `<TIMESTAMP>`\n  - AC3: ISO format (`\"2024-02-19 12:34:56\"`) replaced with `<TIMESTAMP>`\n  - AC4: time-only format (`\"12:34:56\"`) replaced with `<TIMESTAMP>`\n  - AC5: text with no timestamps returned unchanged\n  - Also covers empty input, multiple timestamps in one string, and single-digit day padding\n\n- **`TestComposeNormalizers`** (5 subtests) — verifies R4.3, R4.4:\n  - AC6: two functions applied in order (appendX then appendY → `\"helloXY\"`), with reverse order producing different output (`\"helloYX\"`) to prove sequencing\n  - AC7: zero functions returns input unchanged\n  - Also covers single-function identity and empty input\n\nAll tests use the external `testutils_test` package (D1), table-driven subtests with `t.Parallel()` (D3), and live in a separate file from `difftest_test.go` (D2)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2005,"cache_read_input_tokens":53917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2005},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8644807c-9edf-431a-b50e-24acc54d5ff1","uuid":"5837d617-0995-49b6-811e-38960f275fd1"}
